00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:04.230 align:start position:0%
in a closed session on monday the  eastern based parliament in tulbruck  said it passed a vote of no confidence  in the inter immunity government  but now there are questions about the  transparency of the vote and if it was  even legal  foreign  after reaching quorum for today's  session with 113 mps present a vote of  no confidence was carried out with 89  mps voting to pull confidence from the  unity government the unity government  will continue its work as a caretaker  government  muhammad rayet is an mp he says that for  a no confidence vote to be legal at  least 120 mps must vote for it to be  official  what we saw today was a group of mps who  agreed to carry out a vote they entered  the hall and within minutes announced  that 89 mps voted to pull confidence  from the government there wasn't any  information on who voted how many voted  against and who abstained  the government of national unity came to  power in march it followed a long and  challenging political settlement helped  by the united nations it was tasked with  leading the country until nationwide  elections can take place in december  the move by the parliament to vote on a  no-confidence motion is not in libya's  interest the parliamentary government  should be cooperating and intensifying  their efforts to provide the right  conditions for holding elections  after years of conflict libyans were  beginning to feel hopeful that things  were getting better but now with clear  signs of political divisions emerging  that feeling may start to fade away and  put into question if elections can be  held as scheduled malik trainer al  jazeera tripoli
 

